  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Farmers&apos; Needs Assessment Food Estate North Sumatra</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An Indonesian government project is being developed to prepare 15,000 hectares of currently infertile and unproductive land on North Sumatra for horticulture, leading to a higher food security, increased access to more healthy nutrition and increased local employment. This Dutch funded study project will provide the necessary insights in the needs and capacities of 200 smallholder farmers living nearby the large horticulture project area, to assess how they may be engaged and empowered to participate in and benefit from that horticulture project.</narrative>
  </description>
